  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 101,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume roughly doubled since August 2026 (610/month Jun to 1180-1260/month Aug-Sep, E-05). A confirmed contributing mechanism: manual-read route completion fell to 88% against a 95% target for 9200 accounts over Aug-Sep (E-01), pushing more accounts onto estimate substitution, which accounts for 41% (1240/3025) of currently disputed bills (E-03). Tariff changes (E-02) and dispute-handling capacity (E-04, within SLA) are ruled out as causes, but this estimate-substitution mechanism does not yet explain the majority (59%, 1785/3025) of disputed bills, which used ACTUAL reads (E-03) — a second, unconfirmed billing-pipeline mechanism is driving most of the surge."
