  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 116.0,
  "event_seq": 271,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume roughly doubled since August 2026 (610/590 per month Jun/Jul to 1180/1260 Aug/Sep, E-05), driven by billing-import validation rule BV-17 (deployed 2026-08-01, E-12), which compares raw AMI register values to 12-month m3 consumption history with no unit scaling. Because AMI meters on firmware v4.2 (rolled out June 2026, E-13) report register values in 0.1 m3 instead of m3, BV-17 systematically misflags high consumption at import. This is confirmed for the ESTIMATED-read channel, where 1184 of 1240 disputed bills had a valid AMI read rejected by billing import for high consumption rather than lacking a read at all (E-11); because BV-17 applies at import regardless of read channel (E-12), the same mechanism plausibly also explains disputes on the dominant ACTUAL-read channel (59%, 1785/3025, E-03). Tariff changes (E-02, E-06) and ticket-handling capacity (E-04, within SLA) are ruled out as causes."
 },
